10,0,0,1,0,99,6,MinionPro-Regular,10.0,200.01,554.05,575.95,692.07,554.05,99.93,200.01,36.05,"vehicles are shown in Fig 5 . The following are the steps in the publication of access control pol- icies in BC. • In step 1, the administrator sends an “access control policy” creation request to the BSM. Then, the BSM initiates a “T.publish” transaction. • In step 2, BSM sends “T.publish” to the smart contract. Then, the smart contract validates the administrator’s identity. • In step 3, after successful authentication, the access control policy is saved in BC. • In step 4, the smart contract returns a message i.e., “block added to the BC successfully” to the BSM."
